    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use OpenAI as the text embedding provider for the `embed_text.py` script. It seems like the most straightforward choice. Now, I need to make sure the OpenAI identifier is clearly integrated into the code. I'm focusing on that next.\n\n\n**Defining OpenAI Integration**\n\nI've got the `embed_text.py` script's foundation in place. I'm focusing on integrating the OpenAI client now, specifically handling the API key securely with an environment variable, and the essential steps to generate embeddings with their chosen model. I will be incorporating the import statement and model specification as well.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863813325,
          "start": 1789863811631
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc325a2f001pqNOk8IbEYs0BC",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc325564001yjLaSActPaOVuw",
      "session_id": "ses_f43cdab20ffeHj7x2XIWtevsuk",
      "time_created": 1789863811631,
      "time_updated": 1789863813326
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "7lXtMNgkSa6QeEUS",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\ndef get_text_embedding(text: str) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates an embedding vector for a given text string using OpenAI.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The input text string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of floats representing the embedding vector.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = OpenAI(\n        api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\n    )\n    \n    response = client.embeddings.create(\n        input=[text],\n        model=\"text-embedding-ada-002\"\n    )\n    return response.data[0].embedding\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    example_text = \"This is an example sentence for embedding.\"\n    embedding = get_text_embedding(example_text)\n    print(f\"Embedding for '{example_text}': {embedding[:5]}...\") # Print first 5 dimensions\n    print(f\"Embedding dimension: {len(embedding)}\")\n",
            "filePath": "embed_text.py"
          },
